Right, I complicated myself unnecessarily. I should have defined the
"su'o(n)mei" first, and only then the "(n)mei".

"su'o(pa)mei" is true of anything.

"su'o(n+1)mei":

A are at least n+1 iff there's X among A and Y among A such that X are
at least n and Y are not among X

Then "su'e(n)mei":

A are at most n iff A are not at least n+1

